31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$3,085</a></td><td>Triple-row pavé + cathedral. Maximum rose gold fire.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Milgrain Lace Pavé Platinum</strong></td><td>Platinum</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/milgrain-lace-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-315054?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$3,250</a></td><td>Milgrain lace pavé in platinum. Vintage + lifetime metal.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Gallery Collection Rolled Micropavé RG (3/8 ct.)</strong></td><td>14k Rose Gold</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/the-gallery-collection-rolled-micropave-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-3-8-ct-tw-item-203584?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$3,365</a></td><td>Rolled micro-pavé. Densest Rose Gold pavé in current inventory.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Gallery Collection Knife Edge Micropavé RG (3/8 ct.)</strong></td><td>14k Rose Gold</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/the-gallery-collection-knife-edge-micropave-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-3-8-ct-tw-item-203589?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$3,645</a></td><td>Gallery Collection knife-edge micro-pavé.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Riviera Pavé Platinum (5/8 ct.)</strong></td><td>Platinum</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/riviera-pave-diamond-engagement-ring-in-platinum-5-8-ct-tw-item-195064?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$3,655</a></td><td>Riviera Pavé 5/8 ct in platinum. Lifetime fire.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>French Pavé Platinum (1 ct.)</strong></td><td>Platinum</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/french-pave-diamond-engagement-ring-in-platinum-1-ct-tw-item-194406?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$3,925</a></td><td>Full 1 ct French pavé in platinum. Dense sparkle across whole band.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Gallery Collection Knife Edge Micropavé Platinum</strong></td><td>Platinum</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/the-gallery-collection-knife-edge-micropave-diamond-engagement-ring-in-platinum-3-8-ct-tw-item-194036?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$4,465</a></td><td>Gallery Collection knife-edge micro-pavé in platinum.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Blue Nile Studio Imperial Micropavé (CEILING)</strong></td><td>Platinum</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/blue-nile-studio-imperial-micropave-diamond-engagement-ring-in-platinum-3-8-ct-tw-item-195066?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$4,850</a></td><td>Market ceiling. 3/8 ct imperial micro-pavé + platinum. Max fire.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** 60+ pavé settings run from $1,190 to $4,850 for marquise. The $1,190 Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis Pavé is the entry floor. The $1,325 Petite Micropavé is our micro-pavé baseline. The $1,895 Six-Prong Petite Pavé Platinum is our lifetime pick. The $4,850 Imperial Micropavé Platinum is the max-fire ceiling. Every ring above accepts a marquise centre — the stone shape is selected separately at order.

[![Marquise cut pavé engagement ring in 14k white gold with pavé diamonds set along the band shown from the side showing the pavé profile against a white backdrop](/images/marquise-pave-engagement-ring-white-gold-side-profile.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=pave&ShapeID=Marquise&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

## 5 Details That Add Fire on a Marquise Pavé Ring

**The 5 details below are the whole fire-engineering framework for pavé settings.** Each detail adds measurable sparkle. Stack all five and the ring reads 30–40% brighter than a baseline pavé at the same price point.

### Detail 1 — Micro-Pavé Over Standard Pavé

Standard pavé uses accent stones of 1.5–2.0 mm. Micro-pavé uses stones of 0.8–1.2 mm. Smaller stones means more stones per mm of band, which means more individual flashes as the ring moves in light. Micro-pavé delivers 40–60% more scintillation events per minute than standard pavé at the same pavé coverage.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Pavé Style</th><th>Stone Size</th><th>Stones per mm</th><th>Fire Score (/10)</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Standard pavé</strong></td><td>1.5–2.0 mm</td><td>8–12</td><td>6/10</td><td>Baseline. Larger flashes, fewer per mm.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Micro-pavé</strong></td><td>0.8–1.2 mm</td><td>18–25</td><td>9/10</td><td>Our pick. Finer flashes, more density.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>French pavé (fish-tail)</strong></td><td>1.2–1.8 mm</td><td>12–18</td><td>8/10</td><td>Dense fire with fish-tail prong detail.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Scalloped pavé</strong></td><td>1.5–2.0 mm</td><td>8–12</td><td>7/10</td><td>Vintage profile with scalloped prong tops.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Shared prong</strong></td><td>1.5–2.0 mm</td><td>12–18</td><td>7/10</td><td>More diamond visible, fewer prongs between stones.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** Micro-pavé is our default recommendation for buyers who prioritise fire. The [Petite Micropavé at $1,325](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-micropave-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-1-10-ct-tw-item-195402?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) delivers 20+ stones per mm at an entry-tier price. Standard pavé still works if the aesthetic is cleaner, less-busy sparkle.

### Detail 2 — Shared-Prong Setting Over Individual Prongs

Standard pavé uses two prongs per accent stone (so 20 stones = 40 prongs). Shared-prong (also called "common prong") uses one prong between every pair of accent stones (20 stones = 21 prongs). Less metal visible between stones = more diamond showing = more fire per mm.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Prong Style</th><th>Prong Count</th><th>Metal Visible Between Stones</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Individual prong (standard)</strong></td><td>2 per stone</td><td>High</td><td>Default on cheap pavé. Pavé reads segmented.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Shared prong (common prong)</strong></td><td>1 between pairs</td><td>Low</td><td>Our pick. Pavé reads continuous. See <a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/common-prong-diamond-pave-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-310923?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">Common Prong Pavé WG at $2,090</a>.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Fish-tail (French pavé)</strong></td><td>V-shape between stones</td><td>Minimal</td><td>Minimal metal between stones. Classic French pavé look.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Channel-set</strong></td><td>No prongs — stones in channel</td><td>Only above/below</td><td>Highest security, lowest fire — channels block side light.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** Shared-prong is the fire-maximiser default. Fish-tail (French pavé) is the second choice for buyers who want a classic Parisian-style ring. Individual prongs save $50–$100 on setting cost but cost 20–30% of visible fire.

### Detail 3 — Pavé Coverage: Full Eternity vs 3/4 vs Half

Pavé can cover the top of the band only (half pavé), two-thirds of the band (3/4 pavé), or wrap the whole band (full eternity). Full eternity delivers fire from every angle — including when the hand turns and the inside of the ring shows. 3/4 saves 25–30% on cost but kills fire on the inside third of the finger.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Coverage</th><th>Pavé Extends to</th><th>Fire Direction</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Half pavé (1/4 of shank)</strong></td><td>Top only, near centre</td><td>Front view only</td><td>Entry level. Fire reads from direct front only.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>3/4 pavé</strong></td><td>Top + sides, not bottom</td><td>Front + side views</td><td>Industry standard. Fire from everyday angles.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Full eternity</strong></td><td>Entire shank 360°</td><td>Every angle including underside</td><td>Our fire-max pick. Reads bright from any angle.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Three-quarter + wrap under centre</strong></td><td>3/4 + hidden halo under centre</td><td>Front + hidden sparkle under centre</td><td>Modern compromise. See <a href="/marquise-hidden-halo-engagement-ring">hidden halo guide</a>.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** Full eternity for buyers who want max fire. 3/4 for buyers who want fire from everyday angles without paying the full-eternity premium. Half pavé is a cost-cut that shows — avoid unless the budget demands it.

[![Marquise cut pavé engagement ring in 14k white gold shown from above with pavé diamonds along the band and classic silhouette against a white backdrop](/images/marquise-pave-engagement-ring-white-gold-top-view.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=pave&ShapeID=Marquise&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

### Detail 4 — Platinum Over Gold Under the Pavé

The metal under the accent stones reflects light back up through the pavé. Platinum reflects 90% of visible light. 14k white gold reflects 75%. 14k yellow gold reflects 65%. For the same pavé spec, platinum reads 15–20% brighter than gold. This is why high-end pavé is almost always platinum.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Metal Under Pavé</th><th>Light Reflection</th><th>Fire Brightness</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Platinum</strong></td><td>90%</td><td>Highest</td><td>Our fire pick. 60% denser than gold, 25% brighter under pavé.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>14k White Gold</strong></td><td>75%</td><td>Second</td><td>Acceptable. Rhodium plating keeps the reflection high in year one.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>14k Yellow Gold</strong></td><td>65%</td><td>Warm but less bright</td><td>Warm aesthetic. Pavé reads softer, less fire.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>14k Rose Gold</strong></td><td>70%</td><td>Warm, moderate</td><td>Rose-pink glow under pavé. Trendy but softer fire than white or platinum.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** Platinum base for max fire. White gold for 85% of the platinum fire at 60% of the metal cost. Yellow or rose gold for warm aesthetic over fire priority. The [Six-Prong Petite Pavé in Platinum at $1,895](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/six-prong-petite-pave-diamond-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194944?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is our platinum pick in the mid-tier.

### Detail 5 — Stone Count Density Per mm of Band

The sweet spot for pavé fire is 18–25 stones per linear mm of band. Below 15/mm the stones look spaced out and the band reads "mostly metal with a few diamonds." Above 28/mm the stones are too small (0.6mm or less) to flash individually — they blur into a continuous shimmer that reads as a bright metal surface rather than individual diamonds.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Density (stones/mm)</th><th>Stone Size Needed</th><th>Visual Effect</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Under 15/mm</strong></td><td>&gt;2.0 mm each</td><td>Spaced-out, segmented</td><td>Avoid. Looks like budget pavé.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>15–18/mm</strong></td><td>1.5–1.8 mm each</td><td>Standard pavé density</td><td>Industry baseline. Clean fire.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>18–25/mm (SWEET SPOT)</strong></td><td>1.0–1.4 mm each</td><td>Peak fire — distinct flashes</td><td>Our target. Each stone flashes individually.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>25–28/mm</strong></td><td>0.7–1.0 mm each</td><td>Dense micro-pavé</td><td>Fine shimmer. Fire blurs together.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Over 28/mm</strong></td><td>&lt;0.7 mm each</td><td>Metallic shimmer, not diamond</td><td>Over-set. Reads as bright metal, not diamonds.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** 18–25 stones per mm is the fire sweet spot. Count the stones on the retailer's 360° video over a 10mm section — if the count is in the sweet spot, the fire will read right. If outside, pick a different ring.

> **"The pavé detail I correct most often with clients is the metal choice. Buyers see a $500 saving by picking yellow gold over platinum and jump at it. Then the ring arrives and the pavé reads 20% less bright than they expected. That $500 saving costs the whole fire upgrade they paid for. For pavé-focused buyers, platinum is non-negotiable. Save on the centre stone grade if you have to — not on the metal under the pavé."** — Farzana Hasan, GIA Diamond Expert

## The Fire-Density Formula

**The Fire-Density Formula is how I calculate expected fire output on any pavé ring before I quote a client.** The formula multiplies four variables: stone count, stone size, metal reflection, and coverage angle. Higher output on any variable raises the final fire score.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Range</th><th>Fire Weight</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Stones per mm (density)</strong></td><td>8–28</td><td>35% of fire score</td><td>Biggest fire driver. Micro-pavé wins.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Stone size uniformity</strong></td><td>Mixed vs matched</td><td>15%</td><td>Matched stones = cleaner fire. Mixed = sparkle noise.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Metal reflection coefficient</strong></td><td>65–90%</td><td>25%</td><td>Platinum wins. Yellow gold loses 25% fire vs platinum.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Pavé coverage angle</strong></td><td>120° (half) to 360° (eternity)</td><td>25%</td><td>Full eternity catches light from every angle.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** The Fire-Density Formula says: pick micro-pavé (density boost), platinum (reflection boost), full-eternity (coverage boost), and matched stone sizes (uniformity boost). Stack all four and the ring reads 2x brighter than a basic half-pavé 14k gold setup.

[![Marquise cut pavé engagement ring in 14k white gold with micro-pavé band showing dense stone pattern from above against a white backdrop](/images/marquise-pave-engagement-ring-white-gold-micropave-band.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=pave&ShapeID=Marquise&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

## The Micro-Pavé Durability Trade-Off

**Micro-pavé delivers more fire. It also drops more stones over time.** Smaller accent stones (0.8–1.2 mm) sit in shallower micro-prong seats. Normal wear loosens them faster than standard pavé. Over 5 years, micro-pavé drops 5–10% of accents. Standard pavé drops 2–5%. The fire premium costs the maintenance premium.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Pavé Style</th><th>5-Year Drop Rate</th><th>Re-Set Visits Needed</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Standard pavé (1.5–2mm)</strong></td><td>2–5%</td><td>1 across ring life</td><td>Low maintenance. Occasional drop.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Micro-pavé (0.8–1.2mm)</strong></td><td>5–10%</td><td>2–3 across ring life</td><td>Our pick for fire. Budget for free retailer re-sets.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>French pavé (fish-tail)</strong></td><td>3–7%</td><td>1–2 across ring life</td><td>Fish-tail prongs hold tighter than micro-prongs.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Channel-set (no prongs)</strong></td><td>0–2%</td><td>Rare</td><td>Highest security. Lower fire.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** Micro-pavé requires more free retailer re-set visits over time. Most retailers include this service free for the ring's life — confirm at purchase. If you buy from a retailer that charges for prong work, add $200–$400 to the lifetime cost of micro-pavé over standard pavé.

## The Pavé Drop Protocol

**The Pavé Drop Protocol is the maintenance schedule that keeps a pavé ring at full fire output.** Every pavé ring loses stones over time. The protocol minimises the risk by catching drops early, before adjacent stones destabilise.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Interval</th><th>Check</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Every 2 years</strong></td><td>Jeweller inspection of all accent prongs</td><td>Catches loose stones before they drop.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Every 5 years</strong></td><td>Prong re-tightening across the full pavé band</td><td>Prevents gradual drift that causes drops.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>After any hard impact</strong></td><td>Immediate inspection by jeweller</td><td>Door-frame bumps often loosen pavé stones.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>If you notice a missing accent</strong></td><td>Stop wearing immediately + get re-set</td><td>Adjacent stones destabilise within weeks of a drop.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** Set a 2-year calendar reminder the day the ring arrives. Call the retailer that sold it. Most include free inspection for the ring's life. Independent jewellers charge $25–$75 for a full pavé inspection. Compared to $500+ for stone re-set + replacement, it is the cheapest insurance on the ring.

[![Marquise cut pavé engagement ring in 14k rose gold with full-eternity pavé wrapping the band shown from above against a white backdrop](/images/marquise-pave-engagement-ring-rose-gold-full-eternity-pave.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=pave&ShapeID=Marquise&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

## Diamond Pairing Math — 1ct to 3ct Marquise Centre

A pavé setting is only half the ring. Pairing math for the most common marquise centre carat tiers:

