## Pavé vs Solitaire vs Halo vs Three-Stone for Marquise

A pavé is one of four main setting families for marquise. Quick comparison:

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Setting Family</th><th>Setting Cost</th><th>Fire Added</th><th>Visual Carat</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Solitaire</strong></td><td>$790–$2,850</td><td>None (centre only)</td><td>1x stone</td><td>Classic look. See <a href="/marquise-solitaire-engagement-ring">solitaire guide</a>.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Pavé</strong></td><td>$1,190–$4,850</td><td>High across band</td><td>1x stone + pavé fire</td><td>Our fire pick. 60+ options.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Halo</strong></td><td>$1,255–$5,985</td><td>Moderate around centre</td><td>~1.5x stone</td><td>Bigger-looking stone. See <a href="/marquise-halo-engagement-ring">halo guide</a>.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Three-Stone</strong></td><td>$1,620–$24,800</td><td>Moderate (flankers add carat)</td><td>1x centre + flankers</td><td>Symbolic. See <a href="/marquise-three-stone-engagement-ring">three-stone guide</a>.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** Pavé wins on fire-per-dollar. Halo wins on face-up size. Three-stone wins on symbolic meaning. Solitaire wins on classic simplicity. Pick based on which quality matters most — pavé is the top choice if "sparkle across the whole ring" is the goal.

