## How to Verify a Marquise Pavé Before You Buy

Three checks every ring must pass before you commit.

**Check 1 — Count stones per mm on the 360° video.** Pause the video at the clearest side-profile frame. Count the accent stones over a 10mm section of band. Divide by 10. Sweet spot is 18–25/mm. Below 15 = too spaced. Above 28 = too fine.

**Check 2 — Confirm pavé coverage matches the listing.** Half pavé covers 25% of the shank. 3/4 covers 60–75%. Full eternity covers 100%. If the listing says "pavé" without specifying coverage, ask the retailer or watch the video from every angle to confirm.

**Check 3 — Confirm the retailer offers free lifetime re-set service.** Pavé stones drop. The service policy decides whether that costs $0 or $500+ across the ring's life. [IGI](https://www.igi.org/) and [GIA 4Cs](https://4cs.gia.edu/) both certify loose stones only — the retailer handles pavé maintenance, not the certification lab.

I run these three checks before I quote any client on a pavé ring. The pavé is beautiful when density, coverage, and service all align. It is a $1,500 wasted investment when any one of those three fails.

